            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Erin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used half as much soy sauce (actually Bragg's Amino Acids - GF) based on other reviews. Might even cut it a little more next time. Replaced mayo with coconut milk to make it vegan. Also used fresh lime juice instead of lemon since that's what I had on hand. Processed in the Vitamix for an amazing texture. Delish!",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-15T04:56:06.573Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ms Jean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very easy to pull together and so delicious! I had it with garlic chicken spring rolls, but it is so versatile. Could be served over pasta, with chicken tenders or as a veggie dip. Only added a few pinches of cayenne pepper, and used Miracle Whip in place of the mayo and it worked great. UPDATE 5/15: Added to angel hair pasta (with a little pasta water to make a creamy sauce), sauteed veggies (onions, mushrooms, broccoli, summer squash). Topped with sea salt, cracked black pepper, red pepper flakes, chopped scallions and parmesan cheese. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-26T10:22:15.787Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Elizabeth"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very good, especially on red peppers, Used lite coconut milk instead of mayo and lime juice as well as lemon. Also added Siracha hot sauce for some kick.",
            "datePublished": "2012-04-30T20:25:01.940Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jennifer Martens"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My stars should be higher! Only reason I gave it a 4 was because it was too much soy for my taste. I also did as another reviewer and substituted may for coconut milk. Redid another batch w/ half the soy sauce and doubled the (coconut for mayo) mixed both batches (too salty one) w/ remade one... awesome! I used it as a topping to rice w. veggies AND as a dipping sauce w/ raw veggies. I loved this and will be doing it again. It was so easy to make. The longer its refrigerated the better",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-21T11:45:17.413Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "locamocha"
            },
            "reviewBody": "putting peanut sauce on everything! I used soy milk instead of mayo and added some cayenne pepper, quite an amazing sauce",
            "datePublished": "2014-03-31T17:16:47.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sgtamos"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this &amp; had such high hopes. I tasted after each ingredient was added--halved the soy/tamari sauce (see end note), and garlic was last. It was nearly perfect until I added the garlic. That made it taste so gross. I was able to salvage it with the addition of quite a few other items, but if i make this again, i will omit the garlic &amp; add a little Hot chili sesame oil. As written, It is 3 stars for me. With my salvaging, it was 4-5 stars. ***Also, to make it gluten-free, I subbed tamari sauce for thr soy sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-05T00:51:14.227Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SHARRADOG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a perfect sauce for some salad rolls to encourage my kids to make their own healthy food and eat it. My 3 year old did eat some salad roll but mostly used his finger to dip and eat this sauce. I used plain yoghurt instead of the mayo, and cut the sugar to about a tbsp. I would make this again. It is runny, which was fine with me, but if you are expecting a more traditional thick dip you might want to thicken with something.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-08T17:50:21.623Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Maureen Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just put this in the fridge to chill, but I can't stop licking the bowl. It is delicious! So easy, and made with ingredients I had on hand. I added 1/4 tsp Thai red curry powder, just to see how I'd like it--good and not overpowering. I'll be eating this on everything!",
            "datePublished": "2011-08-14T11:43:34.297Z"
          },
